# ============================================================
# Lesson 08 — func
#
# Keyword of this lesson: func
#
# Run it:
#     python3 juru.py examples/guide/08_func.jr
#
# func gives a piece of code a NAME. Write it once, call it as
# many times as you like, with different values each time.
# ============================================================

# Define once:
func cheer(team) {
    say("Go " + team + "!")
}

# Call as often as you want:
cheer("Red")
cheer("Blue")
cheer("Gold")

# A func can take several arguments, separated by commas:
func rhyme(animal, sound) {
    say("The " + animal + " says " + sound)
}
rhyme("cow", "moo")
rhyme("cat", "meow")

# A func with no arguments is fine too:
func hello() {
    say("hello!")
}
hello()

# A func that only prints is nice for show; the next lesson
# teaches return — funcs that hand a VALUE back.
